[size=5][b]No Diesel - Steam Only[/b][/size]

[i]Hyce made me do it.[/i]

The valley is going back to steam. No more DE2 waiting at every station: the diesels are gone, and only steam spawns.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Steam-only station spawns.[/b] Stations only spawn steam locomotives: the S282 with tender and the S060. A station that only had diesels spawns an S060 instead.
[*][b]Modded steam supported.[/b] Custom Car Loader steam locomotives spawn too. The VR Class Jk3 is included by default; add more by livery ID in [i]steam_ids.txt[/i].
[*][b]Steam start.[/b] A new career with the tutorial skipped starts with the S060 license (and the Jk3's S080 license with Custom Licenses installed) instead of the DE2.
[*][b]No diesel licenses for sale.[/b] DE2, DE6, DH4 and DM3 can't be bought, and the Career Manager tells you why. Edit [i]blocked_licenses.txt[/i] to change the list.
[*][b]Spawn log.[/b] The UMM log lists what every station spawns, before and after filtering.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Unity Mod Manager 0.27.3+
[*]Optional: Custom Car Loader (modded locomotives), Custom Licenses (Jk3's S080 license)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Existing saves keep their licenses; only new careers get the steam start.
[*]The tutorial is built around the DE2 and still grants it. Skip it for a pure steam start.
[*]Locomotives already standing in your save stay until the game clears them.
[*]Garage and restoration locomotives and the sandbox comms-radio spawner are not filtered.
[*]Use either this or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/derailvalley/mods/853]Steam Start[/url] for the starting licenses, not both.
[*]Multiplayer: only the host spawns station locomotives, so the mod is marked host-side. Not yet tested in multiplayer; feedback welcome.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Goes well with[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/derailvalley/mods/1755]Realistic Firing[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/derailvalley/mods/1334]VR Class Jk3[/url]
[/list]

